## Model card

- **Name:** Gemini 2.5, without a variant suffix.
- **Short description:** The name identifies a family, not a sufficiently specified checkpoint for this report. Google's catalog distinguishes Pro, Flash and Flash-Lite, alongside specialized variants. [Official model catalog](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models)
- **Provider / access / IDs:** Verified examples are `gemini-2.5-pro` and `gemini-2.5-flash`; no distinct unsuffixed `gemini-2.5` API model or Zen Free ID verified. [Pro documentation](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models/gemini-2.5-pro), [Flash documentation](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models/gemini-2.5-flash)
- **Release / knowledge:** No exact checkpoint resolved, so no single release or cutoff assigned.
- **Context window:** Variant-dependent; not assigned to the bare family name.
- **Modalities:** The family includes multimodal models, but a single endpoint capability contract is unresolved.
- **Pricing (2026-10-07):** No independently verified price for the unsuffixed identifier. Pro and Flash tariffs must not be blended.
- **Architecture:** Proprietary family; no unique parameter count or checkpoint established for this entry.

### Raw benchmarks found

The Google technical report evaluates named Pro and Flash models separately. Their benchmark results cannot establish a third, unsuffixed model's performance. [Publisher technical report](https://storage.googleapis.com/deepmind-media/gemini/gemini_v2_5_report.pdf?pubDate=20250702)

For an exact unsuffixed model: no verified public score found for agent/tool use, reasoning, coding, multimodal understanding or long-context retrieval. This is an identity-resolution exclusion, not a claim that the Gemini 2.5 family lacks evaluations.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

Not assigned. Retain this entry as excluded until an authoritative provider mapping identifies the intended variant and version. Existing Pro and Flash reports are separate records; this file does not copy or average them.

